<title>SINGAPORE: Natsteel Broadway net profit up 33.1 pct.</title>
<headline>Natsteel Broadway net profit up 33.1 pct.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-03-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31, 1996</p>
<p>	   (in millions of Singapore dollars unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit		   13.06 vs    9.81</p>
<p>    Dividend (percent)	  5.00 vs     nil</p>
<p>    Group share (cents)	12.20 vs    9.70</p>
<p>    Turnover		    101.66 vs   88.17</p>
<p>    Interest income	     0.30 vs    0.09</p>
<p>    Profits from associates   1.17 vs    0.74</p>
<p>    Interest (expense)	  0.29 vs    0.63</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit	     14.81 vs   10.76</p>
<p>    Tax			     1.18 vs    0.94</p>
<p>    Minority interests (loss) 0.58 vs    nil</p>
<p>    Dividend payment date     June 24, 1997</p>
<p>    Books closing date	  June 12, 1997</p>
<p>Note - China-based NatSteel Brodway is an integrated contract manufacturer of plastic and metal components for electronics products. Figures for 1995 are proforma as the group was formed only in 1996, listing in Singapore in October.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 870 3199)</p>
</text>
